1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,690
Welcome to Lesson 3.2: Eligibility Checks.

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:12,590
Each month, before you start working on a CCM patient,

3
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,750
confirm that the patient is still eligible.

4
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:17,956
There are four criteria.

5
00:00:18,233 --> 00:00:20,635
The patient is still in the facility.

6
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:25,628
The CCM condition is a chronic condition that the patient has.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,920
The condition is managed with medication.

8
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,828
And the patient's profile is active in Practice Fusion.

9
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,385
In the last lesson,

10
00:00:35,435 --> 00:00:39,826
you located the patient's profile in the three systems you'll use.

11
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:45,944
PointClickCare, ThoroughCare, and Practice Fusion.

12
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:49,791
Before you start working on the patient,

13
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:53,348
make sure they're still eligible for the CCM program.

14
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,999
CCM, or Chronic Care Management,

15
00:00:56,049 --> 00:01:01,586
is a service for elderly patients who live in skilled nursing facilities,

16
00:01:01,636 --> 00:01:02,698
or SNFs.

17
00:01:02,967 --> 00:01:05,185
There are four eligibility criteria.

18
00:01:05,235 --> 00:01:07,957
You check the first three in PointClickCare,

19
00:01:08,007 --> 00:01:10,725
and the last one in Practice Fusion.

20
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:15,403
The first criterion: the patient is still in the facility.

21
00:01:15,453 --> 00:01:19,491
Not discharged, not in the hospital, and not deceased.

22
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:23,250
Start with the resident banner, at the top of the page.

23
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,637
It shows the patient's general information: name,

24
00:01:26,687 --> 00:01:29,673
date of birth, physician, and location.

25
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,405
Then check the Status.

26
00:01:42,455 --> 00:01:46,955
It should be Current, meaning the patient is in the facility right now.

27
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:50,121
Active, or In-house, means the same thing.

28
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,627
Next, open the Census tab.

29
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,938
It shows the patient's insurance and census history,

30
00:01:57,988 --> 00:02:00,695
with the most recent entry at the top.

31
00:02:06,433 --> 00:02:09,803
Here, the latest entry is from August 18,

32
00:02:09,853 --> 00:02:13,805
2026: Private Pay, with the status Active.

33
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:16,935
Active means the patient is in the facility.

34
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:23,272
If the latest status is Stop Billing, Hospital Leave,

35
00:02:23,322 --> 00:02:27,416
or Hospital, the patient isn't in the facility right now.

36
00:02:27,667 --> 00:02:32,062
For this patient, the latest status is Active, so you can move on.

37
00:02:38,367 --> 00:02:40,547
Then open the MDS tab.

38
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,957
MDS stands for Minimum Data Set.

39
00:02:43,007 --> 00:02:48,407
It's an assessment the facility completes for each resident every three months,

40
00:02:48,457 --> 00:02:50,356
on a quarterly basis.

41
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:54,927
It assesses the patient's basic functions: whether they can walk alone,

42
00:02:54,977 --> 00:02:57,924
and whether they need help with daily activities,

43
00:02:57,974 --> 00:03:00,932
such as showering, eating, and toileting.

44
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:08,036
For eligibility, you only need the most recent MDS, at the top of the list.

45
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:11,196
Routine assessments are Quarterly or Annual.

46
00:03:13,167 --> 00:03:14,685
But there are exceptions.

47
00:03:14,735 --> 00:03:17,258
When a patient is about to be discharged,

48
00:03:17,308 --> 00:03:21,836
the facility completes one final assessment before the discharge.

49
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:27,501
Its description starts with Discharge, such as Discharge Return Anticipated,

50
00:03:27,551 --> 00:03:30,582
or Discharge Return Not Anticipated.

51
00:03:32,133 --> 00:03:35,891
The most recent MDS must not be a discharge assessment,

52
00:03:35,941 --> 00:03:38,537
even if it's still In Progress.

53
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:41,460
If it is, the patient may already have left,

54
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:44,171
and the status just hasn't been updated yet.

55
00:03:44,221 --> 00:03:46,704
Or the patient is about to leave.

56
00:03:46,967 --> 00:03:50,808
In that case, don't work on the patient, to be on the safe side.

57
00:03:51,067 --> 00:03:58,066
Here, the most recent MDS is the October 7, 2026 Annual assessment, In Progress.

58
00:03:58,116 --> 00:04:00,416
It isn't a discharge.

59
00:04:01,267 --> 00:04:04,372
So, to confirm the patient is still in the facility,

60
00:04:04,422 --> 00:04:07,118
check three places in PointClickCare.

61
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:10,399
The Status in the resident banner: Current.

62
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:21,976
The Census tab: the latest status isn't Stop Billing,

63
00:04:22,026 --> 00:04:26,573
Hospital Leave, or anything else that means the patient is away.

64
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:39,634
And the MDS tab: the most recent assessment isn't a discharge.

65
00:04:40,633 --> 00:04:43,924
All three confirm that this patient is in the facility.

66
00:04:43,974 --> 00:04:46,065
That's the first criterion.

67
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:50,974
The second criterion: the CCM condition is

68
00:04:51,024 --> 00:04:55,035
a chronic condition that the patient actually has.

69
00:04:55,767 --> 00:04:58,858
When you receive the patient's information,

70
00:04:58,908 --> 00:05:02,938
it includes the ICD-10 code of the CCM condition.

71
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,873
Here, it's I10.

72
00:05:05,133 --> 00:05:07,586
Because this is a chronic care program,

73
00:05:07,636 --> 00:05:12,462
confirm two things: the condition is on the patient's active diagnosis list,

74
00:05:12,512 --> 00:05:14,758
and it's chronic, not acute.

75
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:24,606
The patient's active conditions are in the MED DIAG tab.

76
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,185
It lists each active condition, with its ICD-10 code.

77
00:05:31,467 --> 00:05:34,264
Look for the code of the CCM condition.

78
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:41,686
Here it is: I10, Essential (primary) hypertension.

79
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:45,633
Hypertension is a chronic condition, not an acute one,

80
00:05:45,683 --> 00:05:47,973
such as a urinary tract infection.

81
00:05:48,023 --> 00:05:49,780
So you can move on.

82
00:06:04,267 --> 00:06:08,846
The third criterion: the condition is managed with medication.

83
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:12,117
This patient's CCM condition is hypertension,

84
00:06:12,167 --> 00:06:16,978
so they must be taking at least one medication for hypertension.

85
00:06:19,367 --> 00:06:21,275
You'll find this in the ORDERS tab,

86
00:06:21,325 --> 00:06:24,404
which lists all of the patient's active orders.

87
00:06:24,667 --> 00:06:26,239
First, filter the list.

88
00:06:26,289 --> 00:06:28,220
Open Display Filters.

89
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:33,488
Under Order Category, untick every category except Pharmacy.

90
00:06:37,467 --> 00:06:38,958
Then click Search.

91
00:06:39,833 --> 00:06:44,160
Now the list shows the medications the patient is currently taking.

92
00:06:44,433 --> 00:06:48,555
Look for at least one medication for the CCM condition.

93
00:06:52,633 --> 00:06:57,079
Here, the patient takes diltiazem HCl, 60 mg.

94
00:06:57,333 --> 00:07:02,604
Its directions show what it's for: give 1 tablet by mouth two times a day,

95
00:07:02,654 --> 00:07:03,179
for HTN.

96
00:07:03,229 --> 00:07:05,117
That's hypertension.

97
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:08,154
So the condition is managed with medication.

98
00:07:08,204 --> 00:07:10,394
That's the third criterion.

99
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,646
So far, the patient is in the facility,

100
00:07:14,696 --> 00:07:19,500
the CCM condition is chronic, and it's managed with medication.

101
00:07:25,667 --> 00:07:30,663
The fourth criterion: the patient's profile is active in Practice Fusion.

102
00:07:30,933 --> 00:07:34,439
Practice Fusion is the platform where you upload the encounter,

103
00:07:34,489 --> 00:07:37,365
and submit it to the insurance for billing.

104
00:07:38,933 --> 00:07:46,130
To check, search for the patient by date of birth, in the format MM/DD/YYYY.

105
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:51,027
The results show every patient with that date of birth.

106
00:07:54,033 --> 00:07:58,674
An inactive profile is marked Inactive, and its name is grayed out.

107
00:08:04,133 --> 00:08:08,783
Make sure the patient's own profile is active, with no Inactive label.

108
00:08:09,033 --> 00:08:12,647
Here, it's active, so the fourth criterion is met.

109
00:08:14,633 --> 00:08:18,390
This patient meets all four eligibility criteria.

110
00:08:18,667 --> 00:08:23,825
In PointClickCare, the patient is in the facility: the Status is Current,

111
00:08:23,875 --> 00:08:28,535
the census is Active, and the latest MDS isn't a discharge.

112
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:35,061
The CCM condition, hypertension, is a chronic condition on the diagnosis list.

113
00:08:44,767 --> 00:08:48,504
It's managed with medication: in the filtered Orders tab,

114
00:08:48,554 --> 00:08:51,995
the patient takes diltiazem for hypertension.

115
00:08:56,933 --> 00:09:00,561
And the patient's profile is active in Practice Fusion.

116
00:09:00,833 --> 00:09:03,693
Now you're ready to start working on the patient.

117
00:09:04,867 --> 00:09:06,125
To recap.

118
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:10,957
First, the patient is still in the facility: the Status is Current,

119
00:09:11,007 --> 00:09:16,476
the latest census status is Active, and the latest MDS isn't a discharge.

120
00:09:16,733 --> 00:09:22,157
Second, the CCM condition is chronic, and it's on the MED DIAG list.

121
00:09:22,433 --> 00:09:27,344
Third, the condition is managed with medication, in the pharmacy orders.

122
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:31,650
And fourth, the patient's profile is active in Practice Fusion.

123
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:36,622
That's the end of Lesson 3.2.

124
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:42,049
Next, in Lesson 3.3: formulating the care plan's problem note.
